<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Peakon Engagement Report — Logistics Design & Research</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    body {
      font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Inter", "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      background: #f7f7f5;
      color: #1a1a1a;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    /* ── Nav ── */
    nav {
      position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background: rgba(247,247,245,0.92);
      backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e0;
      padding: 0 40px;
    }
    nav ul { display: flex; list-style: none; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; }
    nav ul li a {
      display: block; padding: 16px 20px;
      font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: #666;
      text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
      transition: color .15s, border-color .15s;
    }
    nav ul li a:hover { color: #1a1a1a; border-color: #1a1a1a; }

    .page { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 72px 40px 120px; }

    .eyebrow {
      display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #999; margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
    h1 { font-size: 48px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.1; color: #111; }
    h2 { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em; color: #111; }
    h3 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: #111; }

    .hero { margin-bottom: 80px; }
    .hero p.subtitle { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 17px; color: #555; max-width: 580px; }

    /* ── Snapshot cards ── */
    .stats { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 48px; }
    .stat-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e8e8e3; border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px 28px 24px; }
    .stat-card .stat-label { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #999; margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .stat-card .stat-value { font-size: 52px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1; color: #111; }
    .stat-card .stat-value.below { color: #dc2626; }
    .stat-card .stat-meta { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13px; color: #888; }

    section { margin-top: 88px; }
    .section-header { margin-bottom: 36px; }
    .section-header p { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px; color: #666; max-width: 640px; }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       SIMPLE BAR CHART
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .driver-chart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }

    .driver-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 210px 1fr auto;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 14px;
    }
    .driver-name { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500; color: #444; text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }

    .bar-track {
      height: 10px; background: #e8e8e3; border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden;
    }
    .bar-fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 99px; }
    .bar-fill.green  { background: #16a34a; }
    .bar-fill.amber  { background: #f59e0b; }
    .bar-fill.red    { background: #dc2626; }

    .score-meta {
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-end;
      min-width: 80px; gap: 1px;
    }
    .score-main { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: #111; }
    .score-dh   { font-size: 11px; color: #888; }
    .score-gap  { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; }
    .score-gap.pos { color: #16a34a; }
    .score-gap.neg { color: #dc2626; }

    .chart-legend {
      display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-top: 16px; margin-left: 224px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    }
    .legend-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; font-size: 12px; color: #666; }
    .legend-dot  { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }

    /* ════════════════════════════════
       AREA CARDS
    ════════════════════════════════ */
    .cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 24px; }
    .area-card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e8e8e3; border-radius: 20px; overflow: hidden; }

    .area-card-head { padding: 28px 32px 24px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f0f0eb; }
    .tag {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 99px; margin-bottom: 14px;
    }
    .tag.strength { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }
    .tag.focus    { background: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; }
    .tag.watch    { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }

    .driver-info { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 24px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .driver-info h3 { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; padding-top: 4px; }

    /* Score badge pair */
    .score-pair {
      display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 0;
      background: #f7f7f5; border: 1px solid #e8e8e3; border-radius: 12px; overflow: hidden;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .score-cell {
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;
      padding: 12px 18px; gap: 3px;
    }
    .score-cell + .score-cell { border-left: 1px solid #e8e8e3; }
    .score-cell .lbl { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .07em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #aaa; }
    .score-cell .val { font-size: 32px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1; }
    .score-cell .val.green  { color: #16a34a; }
    .score-cell .val.red    { color: #dc2626; }
    .score-cell .val.amber  { color: #d97706; }
    .score-cell .val.muted  { color: #555; }
    .score-cell .sub        { font-size: 11px; color: #aaa; }
    .gap-pill {
      display: inline-block; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700;
      padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 99px; margin-top: 2px;
    }
    .gap-pill.pos { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }
    .gap-pill.neg { background: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; }

    .area-card-head p.signal { margin-top: 14px; font-size: 14px; color: #555; line-height: 1.6; }

    /* ── Question breakdown table ── */
    .area-card-body { padding: 28px 32px; }

    .q-breakdown { margin-bottom: 24px; }
    .q-breakdown-title {
      font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #aaa; margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .q-row {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 56px 56px 64px;
      gap: 10px; align-items: center;
      padding: 10px 14px;
      background: #f9f9f7; border: 1px solid #ebebE6; border-radius: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .q-row:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .q-text { font-size: 13px; color: #333; font-style: italic; line-height: 1.45; }
    .q-score, .q-dh {
      display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 1px;
    }
    .q-score .qlbl, .q-dh .qlbl {
      font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #bbb;
    }
    .q-score .qval {
      font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -.01em; line-height: 1;
    }
    .q-dh .qval { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 600; color: #666; line-height: 1; }
    .qval.green { color: #16a34a; }
    .qval.red   { color: #dc2626; }
    .qval.amber { color: #d97706; }
    .q-gap-pill {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 8px; border-radius: 99px;
    }
    .q-gap-pill.pos { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }
    .q-gap-pill.neg { background: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; }

    /* ── Comments ── */
    .comment-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(255px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; }
    .comment-bubble {
      background: #f9f9f7; border: 1px solid #ebebE6; border-radius: 14px; padding: 16px 18px;
    }
    .comment-bubble blockquote {
      font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.65; color: #333; font-style: italic;
      border: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;
    }
    /* Score dot + label wrapper */
    .score-dot-wrap {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px; margin-bottom: 9px;
    }
    .score-dot-label {
      font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .06em;
      text-transform: uppercase; color: #bbb;
    }
    .score-dot {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%;
      font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .score-dot.high  { background: #dcfce7; color: #15803d; }
    .score-dot.mid   { background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; }
    .score-dot.low   { background: #fee2e2; color: #b91c1c; }
    .score-dot.empty { background: #f3f4f6; color: #9ca3af; }

    .pattern-callout {
      margin-top: 20px; padding: 15px 18px;
      background: #f3f4f6; border-left: 3px solid #9ca3af;
      border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0; font-size: 14px; color: #444;
    }
    .pattern-callout strong { color: #111; }

    .section-divider { height: 1px; background: #eeede8; margin: 20px 0; }

    /* Culture words */
    .culture-words { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 14px; }
    .culture-word {
      padding: 7px 14px; border-radius: 99px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 500;
      border: 1px solid #e0e0db; background: #fff; color: #333;
    }
    .culture-word.positive { border-color: #bbf7d0; background: #f0fdf4; color: #166534; }
    .culture-word.negative { border-color: #fecaca; background: #fff5f5; color: #991b1b; }
    .culture-word.neutral  { border-color: #e5e7eb; background: #f9fafb; color: #374151; }

    footer {
      margin-top: 120px; padding-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e0;
      font-size: 12px; color: #aaa; text-align: center;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="#snapshot">Snapshot</a></li>
    <li><a href="#scores">Driver Scores</a></li>
    <li><a href="#strengths">Relative Strengths</a></li>
    <li><a href="#focus">Focus Areas</a></li>
    <li><a href="#watch">Watch Areas</a></li>
  </ul>
</nav>

<div class="page">

  <!-- Hero -->
  <div class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Peakon · April 2026</span>
    <h1>Peakon Report</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">Logistics Design &amp; Research — eNPS scores, DH benchmarks, question-level breakdowns, and voices from the survey.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Snapshot -->
  <section id="snapshot">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2>Survey Snapshot</h2>
      <p>All scores are <strong>eNPS</strong> (% promoters − % detractors, range −100 to +100). Each driver card shows the sub-question score alongside the DH organisation benchmark.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Engagement eNPS</div>
        <div class="stat-value below">23</div>
        <div class="stat-meta">DH benchmark: 34 &nbsp;·&nbsp; −11 below</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Participation</div>
        <div class="stat-value">68%</div>
        <div class="stat-meta">13 of 19 employees responded</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <div class="stat-label">Comments Submitted</div>
        <div class="stat-value">70</div>
        <div class="stat-meta">Across all drivers and open-ended questions</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Bar chart -->
  <section id="scores">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">All Drivers</span>
      <h2>Driver eNPS Scores</h2>
      <p>eNPS scale: −100 to +100. Bar length reflects score magnitude. DH organisation benchmark shown alongside each score.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="driver-chart" id="driverChart"></div>

    <div class="chart-legend">
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#16a34a"></div>Above DH benchmark</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#f59e0b"></div>Watch — below benchmark</div>
      <div class="legend-item"><div class="legend-dot" style="background:#dc2626"></div>Focus area — significantly below</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════
       RELATIVE STRENGTHS
  ════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="strengths">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#16a34a;">● Relative Strengths</span>
      <h2 style="color:#15803d;">Our best-performing areas</h2>
      <p>These drivers score above the DH organisation benchmark. Peakon's algorithm did not flag any formal team-level strengths (a high bar), but these are the areas where the team is outperforming the organisation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">

      <!-- Freedom of Opinion -->
      <div class="area-card">
        <div class="area-card-head">
          <div class="tag strength">● Above DH benchmark</div>
          <div class="driver-info">
            <h3>Freedom of Opinion</h3>
            <div class="score-pair">
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">Team eNPS</span>
                <span class="val green">62</span>
                <span class="sub">Manager sub</span>
                <span class="gap-pill pos">+7 vs DH</span>
              </div>
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">DH Benchmark</span>
                <span class="val muted">55</span>
                <span class="sub">Org average</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="signal">Manager relationships score strongly above the DH average. The colleague sub-driver (how freely people speak up with peers) sits at 46 — 7 below DH — and is worth monitoring.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-card-body">
          <div class="q-breakdown">
            <div class="q-breakdown-title">Question breakdown</div>
            <div class="q-row">
              <div class="q-text">"My manager values my input."</div>
              <div class="q-score"><span class="qlbl">Team</span><span class="qval green">62</span></div>
              <div class="q-dh"><span class="qlbl">DH</span><span class="qval">55</span></div>
              <span class="q-gap-pill pos">+7</span>
            </div>
            <div class="q-row">
              <div class="q-text">"I feel comfortable voicing my opinion with colleagues."</div>
              <div class="q-score"><span class="qlbl">Team</span><span class="qval amber">46</span></div>
              <div class="q-dh"><span class="qlbl">DH</span><span class="qval">53</span></div>
              <span class="q-gap-pill neg">−7</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="section-divider"></div>
          <div class="comment-grid">
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">10</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"I really appreciate the support my manager provides. My manager values my input, and helps me transform basic ideas into actionable initiatives."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">10</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"My manager generally values my input and design perspective. I feel heard in discussions within the Delivery Flow domain. Overall, there is good openness to my contributions."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot mid">7</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"Yes my manager values my input but there is not much impact."</blockquote>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="pattern-callout">
            <strong>Pattern:</strong> Manager relationships are respectful and open. The gap between feeling heard and seeing visible change ties this driver back to the Recognition and Survey Follow-up gaps.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Autonomy -->
      <div class="area-card">
        <div class="area-card-head">
          <div class="tag strength">● Above DH benchmark</div>
          <div class="driver-info">
            <h3>Autonomy — Flexibility</h3>
            <div class="score-pair">
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">Team eNPS</span>
                <span class="val green">38</span>
                <span class="sub">Flexibility sub</span>
                <span class="gap-pill pos">+2 vs DH</span>
              </div>
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">DH Benchmark</span>
                <span class="val muted">36</span>
                <span class="sub">Org average</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="signal">Work schedule flexibility is valued and the team edges above the DH average. People feel trusted to manage their own time and accommodate personal commitments.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-card-body">
          <div class="q-breakdown">
            <div class="q-breakdown-title">Question breakdown</div>
            <div class="q-row">
              <div class="q-text">"My work schedule is flexible enough to accommodate my family or personal life."</div>
              <div class="q-score"><span class="qlbl">Team</span><span class="qval green">38</span></div>
              <div class="q-dh"><span class="qlbl">DH</span><span class="qval">36</span></div>
              <span class="q-gap-pill pos">+2</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="section-divider"></div>
          <div class="comment-grid">
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">10</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"I feel my work schedule is generally flexible enough. Most of the time I'm able to manage work alongside personal commitments effectively."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">9</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"Yes it mostly is [flexible]. Overall it feels balanced."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot mid">7</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"Schedule is flexible but not [happy with] work from office policy."</blockquote>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="pattern-callout">
            <strong>Pattern:</strong> Flexibility is a genuine point of satisfaction. The in-office policy creates a small friction for some, but the overall sense of autonomy is positive and above the DH norm.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Reward -->
      <div class="area-card">
        <div class="area-card-head">
          <div class="tag strength">● Above DH benchmark</div>
          <div class="driver-info">
            <h3>Reward — Compensation Fairness</h3>
            <div class="score-pair">
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">Team eNPS</span>
                <span class="val green">8</span>
                <span class="sub">Fairness sub</span>
                <span class="gap-pill pos">+6 vs DH</span>
              </div>
              <div class="score-cell">
                <span class="lbl">DH Benchmark</span>
                <span class="val muted">2</span>
                <span class="sub">Org average</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="signal">Compensation feels broadly fair relative to role and responsibility, and the team scores 6 points above the DH average. Note: the <em>clarity</em> of how to progress and get better ratings is a separate, weaker area.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="area-card-body">
          <div class="q-breakdown">
            <div class="q-breakdown-title">Question breakdown</div>
            <div class="q-row">
              <div class="q-text">"I feel I am compensated fairly (e.g. pay and other forms of compensation)."</div>
              <div class="q-score"><span class="qlbl">Team</span><span class="qval green">8</span></div>
              <div class="q-dh"><span class="qlbl">DH</span><span class="qval">2</span></div>
              <span class="q-gap-pill pos">+6</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="section-divider"></div>
          <div class="comment-grid">
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">10</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"I feel my compensation is generally fair and aligned with my role as a Staff Product Designer. It feels broadly consistent with responsibilities and impact."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot high">8</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"I have a general understanding of how the rewards structure works. It is mostly clear in how it relates to role level and performance."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot mid">7</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"Sometimes it's hard to understand the different LTIPs without in-depth reading of the T&Cs."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot mid">5</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"I am not sure what this means."</blockquote>
            </div>
            <div class="comment-bubble">
              <div class="score-dot-wrap"><div class="score-dot low">3</div><span class="score-dot-label">Respondent score (0–10)</span></div>
              <blockquote>"If we are talking about performance reward, no, I have no idea what I need to do to get a better performance rating."</blockquote>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="pattern-callout">
            <strong>Pattern:</strong> The team outperforms the organisation on pay fairness. The frustration is not with pay itself — it's with the opaque mechanics: how to earn a better performance rating, what LTIPs mean, and how to progress. Three of five respondents expressed confusion about the rewards structure.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ════════════════════════════════
       FOCUS AREAS
  ════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section id="focus">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#dc2626;">● Focus Areas</span>
      <h2 style="color:#b91c1c;">Where we need to act</h2>
      <p>Peakon formally identified these as the team's focus areas — drivers with the strongest negative pull on overall engagement, all sitting significantly below the DH benchmark.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cards">

